{
  "title": "PLANKA \u2014 productivity (12,002\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: PLANKA\nDomain: productivity | Scale: medium | Stars: 12,002\nProblem: Teams need a self-hosted, open-source Kanban board tool for collaborative project management without relying on proprietary SaaS solutions. PLANKA provides a Trello-like experience that can be deployed on your own infrastructure.\nTarget users: Software development teams, Project managers, Agile practitioners, Organizations requiring self-hosted project management tools, Small to medium businesses seeking Trello alternatives\nCore features: Collaborative Kanban boards with drag-and-drop interface (projects, boards, lists, cards); Real-time updates and syncing across all connected users; Rich markdown editor for card descriptions; Flexible notifications via 100+ providers; Single sign-on via OpenID Connect (OIDC) integration; Internationalization and multilingual support; REST API with Swagger documentation; Self-hosted Docker deployment\nIntegrations: OpenID Connect (SSO), Docker, Discord (community), 100+ notification providers, TestFlight (iOS Notes app)\nTech stack: React (JavaScript/JSX, SCSS) + Node.js (Sails.js framework) + PostgreSQL + Docker, self-hosted\nKey libraries: concurrently, husky, lint-staged, genversion\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Monorepo structure with separate client and server workspaces managed via npm prefix scripts, enabling independent builds and linting while sharing a single repository.\n- Real-time collaboration is a first-class concern, likely implemented via WebSockets to push board state changes to all connected clients without polling.\n- Self-hostability is a core design principle, with Docker as the primary deployment target and environment-based configuration for flexibility across environments.\n- Fair-code licensing model (source-available with commercial restrictions) combined with a hosted Pro/Enterprise tier represents a sustainable open-core business strategy.",
